GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Position_IntermediaryNetworkEffectsFederation> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Position_IntermediaryNetworkEffectsFederation> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_IntermediaryNetworkEffectsFederation> ;
    narr:childCount "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "d60479f4df57bd74c60ef357e16a3ce7cbb09a43" ;
    narr:narration """This position argues that durable moats in a commodifying-AI market come from [sitting in between — the telephone-company thesis](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_109), grounded in the claim that [the marginal cost of software development is approaching zero](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_105). The supporting arc runs through [rapid commodification of any shown capability](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_119), the warning that [building a better version hands incumbents the blueprint](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_115), and the historical analogy that [a platform can destroy an incumbent without beating it on its own terms](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_111) because [switching costs, not quality, protect the installed base](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_113). The thesis is applied to transcription tools — [commodity players predicted to fade because they don't sit in between](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_117) — and made concrete via [cross-company paid access making each party's copy more valuable](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_125) and [the viral flip: wanting it because you have it](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_127). Tanya sketches the mechanism as [paid graphs gaining permitted interconnect from each other's graphs](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_128), which opens the open problem of [secure, managed federation across organizational graphs](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_158) — hard, per the claim that [LLMs derive value from private context and are weak at this space](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_157). A second, adjacent thesis appears in [charging only for the in-the-middle layer while everything else is free](narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_133).""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_105> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_109> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_111> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_113> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_115> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_117> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_119> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_121> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_125> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_127> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_128> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_133> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_157> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_158> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "One of my operating theses is the telephone company always wins." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_105> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "The marginal cost of software development is asymptotically approaching zero." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_105> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "The, the speed to commodification of a capability" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_119> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Non commodifiable means you're the telephone company. You sit in between, right?" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_119> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "I think Fireflies and Otter are going to go away too" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_117> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "how do you do federation across different organizations graphs in a way that is secure and managed" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_158> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "LLMs are not great at this particular problem space." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_157> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The incumbent-displacement risk is held as conditional, not certain — \"that could happen. I'm not saying they will. They might\" — the thesis admits its own counterfactual." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_117> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The internal-network-effect counterargument is conceded but deflected: data accumulation inside one company is real, yet the claim is a better version can still displace it — the moat question stays open." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_111> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The federation mechanism is spitballed, not settled: permissioning and access issues are explicitly flagged as unsolved, and the cross-org interconnect design remains an open question rather than a committed plan." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_128> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_158> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "A second, distinct thesis rides alongside — serving companies too small for big-firm consulting — which is a market-gap argument, not a network-effects one; the two theses are linked by pricing model, not by the same logic." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_133> ] ;
    narr:writer "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:nitro" .
}